<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">PEFT Methods.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide supplementary experiments with SFT and DPO in Table <a href="#A7.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ PEFT Methods. ‣ G.1 Detailed Study on Llama3.1-8B-Instruct ‣ Appendix G Further Experiments on Emotion Steering ‣ Psychological Steering in LLMs: An Evaluation of Effectiveness and Trustworthiness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. In this Table, we provide two learning rates as well as four different sourcing datasets. Notice that SFT with learning rate <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-4</annotation></semantics></math> trained on <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">EmoTranslate</span> dataset achieves the best overall performance according to the open-ended acc., QA acc., and fluency metrics.</p>
</div>
